WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.470
A chalkboard outside a café:
pop in for a proper brew, love!

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.640
A linguist holds up a lens.

3
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:11.710
First pass: that repeated
p sound, pop, proper.

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.260
Second pass: the word brew.

5
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.990
Third: there's no subject at all.

6
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.300
Then the exclamation mark,
and that friendly love.

7
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:22.180
It's one short sign.

8
00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.240
So why would anyone go
over it again and again,

9
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.940
level by level?

10
00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.100
In this mission, you'll meet
the levels linguists work with,

11
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.870
from sound right up to the whole text.

12
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.100
You'll zoom in on lexis,
the level of word choice,

13
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.460
and ask why a sign says brew and not tea.

14
00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.150
And you'll test it all on an estate
agent's listing for a cottage.

15
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.300
Your mission: explain why
linguists work level by level.
